(5608594, 811849, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kmusser:</b></div><hr/><i> Photo is too blurry and first thought is not of squares but of diamonds. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for taking the time to comment. The depth of field (blur you are referencing) was purposeful and served the purpose of directing the viewer to the intersection of the four squares, the in focus four right angles (square).</td>', 'Originally posted by kmusser: Photo is too blurry and first thought is not of squares but of diamonds.   Thanks for taking the time to comment. The depth of field (blur you are referencing) was purposeful and served the purpose of directing the viewer to the intersection of the four squares, the in focus four right angles (square).', '2009-08-12 03:49:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5608595, 811815, 54645, '<td valign="top">Excellent texture and tones. I can feel the age, although I don''t see any squares, just rectangles upon rectangles. ;) Actually, they are perfect rectangles!</td>', 'Excellent texture and tones. I can feel the age, although I don''t see any squares, just rectangles upon rectangles. ;) Actually, they are perfect rectangles!', '2009-08-12 03:53:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5608599, 811944, 54645, '<td valign="top">Poor Prince Charming! I see the frame as the subject, particularly with the title. I''m not sure why it appears a bit soft, is this same image you were working on last week?<br/> <br/>BTW, the humor is fantastic!</td>', 'Poor Prince Charming! I see the frame as the subject, particularly with the title. I''m not sure why it appears a bit soft, is this same image you were working on last week? BTW, the humor is fantastic!', '2009-08-12 03:59:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5608610, 812043, 54645, '<td valign="top">Yeah, some interesting comments...<br/> <br/>I thought this met the challenge. How many squares do you need?! The pants are framed in a square! The frame itself links the feet to the footprints. The layers of light to dark to light worked out well, yet I can also see why Don called it a jumble. <br/> <br/>Did you shoot this through a window?</td>', 'Yeah, some interesting comments... I thought this met the challenge. How many squares do you need?! The pants are framed in a square! The frame itself links the feet to the footprints. The layers of light to dark to light worked out well, yet I can also see why Don called it a jumble.  Did you shoot this through a window?', '2009-08-12 04:08:36.000000', NULL, 0),
