(5608709, 812043, 60915, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bspurgeon:</b></div><hr/><i> Yeah, some interesting comments...<br/> <br/>I thought this met the challenge. How many squares do you need?! The pants are framed in a square! The frame itself links the feet to the footprints. The layers of light to dark to light worked out well, yet I can also see why Don called it a jumble. <br/> <br/>Did you shoot this through a window? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Ben, kind of, the square is on a glass balustrade, I suppose you''d call it. It surrounds an outdoor cafe/bar. That''s the bottom of the glass edge just above the curb.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by bspurgeon: Yeah, some interesting comments... I thought this met the challenge. How many squares do you need?! The pants are framed in a square! The frame itself links the feet to the footprints. The layers of light to dark to light worked out well, yet I can also see why Don called it a jumble.  Did you shoot this through a window?   Thanks Ben, kind of, the square is on a glass balustrade, I suppose you''d call it. It surrounds an outdoor cafe/bar. That''s the bottom of the glass edge just above the curb. ', '2009-08-12 05:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
