(5613330, 811716, 16912, '<td valign="top">Greetings from Andi via the Critique Club and congratulations on this top ten image!<br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> A well exposed sky and you did a decent job of exposing the rest of the shot though its still a little dark at the edges for me.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> Considering the planter being in the way I think you did a great job of composing this shot but it looks as if it could do with being rotated half a degree to the left.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> Fits the challenge well though it doesn''t ''WOW'' me (I gave it a 6 btw). Now, if there was a low flying aeroplane dead centre this would have ribboned :)<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> My only thought on the technical quality of this shot is maybe some light shadow/highlight or equivalent during post processing to get a little more details at the edges but, after saying that maybe it works better as it is.<br/> <br/><b>Final thoughts:</b> A great shot for the challenge. Maybe you could have squeezed most of this into a square crop? I love the shutters at various staged of being opened/closed.</td>', 'Greetings from Andi via the Critique Club and congratulations on this top ten image! First Impression: A well exposed sky and you did a decent job of exposing the rest of the shot though its still a little dark at the edges for me. Composition: Considering the planter being in the way I think you did a great job of composing this shot but it looks as if it could do with being rotated half a degree to the left. Subject: Fits the challenge well though it doesn''t ''WOW'' me (I gave it a 6 btw). Now, if there was a low flying aeroplane dead centre this would have ribboned :) Technical: My only thought on the technical quality of this shot is maybe some light shadow/highlight or equivalent during post processing to get a little more details at the edges but, after saying that maybe it works better as it is. Final thoughts: A great shot for the challenge. Maybe you could have squeezed most of this into a square crop? I love the shutters at various staged of being opened/closed.', '2009-08-16 17:12:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5613404, 811893, 34938, '<td valign="top">Soon! Finally all of your patience and effort paid off! Congrats on your first ribbon, PB and a great image</td>', 'Soon! Finally all of your patience and effort paid off! Congrats on your first ribbon, PB and a great image', '2009-08-16 19:30:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5613937, 811876, 34938, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scarbrd:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice image! Cool that you and Soon pulled off ribbons shooting the same thing! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Absolutely true! You have had a stellar year Andrew. Well done. Hope to see you in November</td>', 'Originally posted by scarbrd: Nice image! Cool that you and Soon pulled off ribbons shooting the same thing!   Absolutely true! You have had a stellar year Andrew. Well done. Hope to see you in November', '2009-08-17 02:36:21.000000', NULL, 0),
